  "narrative": {
    "overview": "This document covers the compact Chrome action popup in `src/panel/panel.html` and `src/panel/panel.ts`. Its navy utility interface puts listening state, the primary control, and the latest command within a short scan. It records the shipped popup system; other extension surfaces require their own design decisions.\n\nThe popup controls a persistent voice session. Its listening note explains that closing the popup leaves the microphone running. The reviewed default popup measures 340 × 270 CSS pixels.",
    "rules": [],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep listening state and its primary control visible before contextual content.",
      "Do pair status color with explicit text and keep the persistent microphone explanation close to the control.",
      "Do reveal confirmation, vault, error, and help content only when relevant."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't turn the compact popup into a dashboard or introduce a new product-wide identity through this document.",
